; The same three questions, answered a second time by a different part of
; `writ`, so that `modality-cross-check.sh` can compare them. A disagreement is
; a bug in one of them, not a number to adjust.
;
; POLARITY:
;   `possible F` is the SATISFYING set — non-empty means it holds.
;   `never F` and `live F` are COUNTEREXAMPLE sets — EMPTY means it holds.
(load "ct.rules")
(load "deployment.lib.writ")

(satisfies upgrades (and (all-at-healthy r2) (is db.at v2)))

(satisfies never-dark none-healthy)

(satisfies on-r1 (all-at-healthy r1))
(can-reach can-get-to-r1 on-r1)
(trapped can-roll-back can-get-to-r1)

; ---- which decisions cannot be taken back ----
; `one-way` (ct.rules §4) is every edge that leaves its strongly connected
; component: a move after which the situation it left can never be reached
; again. Asked with no goal in mind. Projected onto the move's name, which is
; the column that answers "which step was that".
(relation irreversible (Edge))
(rule (irreversible E) (one-way E S T))
